---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Technical Guide & Overview">
  
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <div class="relative py-12 md:py-16 border-b border-white/5 mb-12 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl">
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-2xl">
      <span class="text-[10px] font-mono tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-technical-amber mb-2 block">Blender Addon Documentation</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-white tracking-tight leading-none mb-4 border-none p-0 mt-0">
        Scene Light Manager
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-zinc-400 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
        A professional, modular Blender extension designed to optimize lighting workflows. Manage scene hierarchies, collection-level overrides, interactive viewport gizmos, and GPU shader previews from a single unified panel.
      </p>
      
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="#features" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-zinc-950 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest font-medium hover:bg-zinc-200 transition-all duration-300">
          Explore Features
        </a>
        <a href="https://kezives.gumroad.com/l/k-tools-mode-highlight" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-white font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest font-medium hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300">
          Gumroad Store
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="features" class="scroll-mt-[120px]"></div>

  <h2>── 1. Architectural Design & Folder Layout ──</h2>
  <p>
    SLM is built under a modular design philosophy that separates Blender's registration lifecycle from UI layouts, operator actions, and custom data schemas.
  </p>
  
  <pre class="scrollbar-custom"><code>k_tools_scene_light_manager/
37: ├── __init__.py               # Registers/unregisters core modules & registers subclasses
38: ├── auto_load.py              # Handles dynamic recursive module detection and registration
39: ├── blender_manifest.toml     # Metadata and platform information for Blender Extensions
40: ├── preferences.py            # Global addon preferences, properties, and the main preference panel
41: │
42: ├── properties/               # Persistent data and RNA properties
43: │   ├── outliner.py           # Custom attributes for outliner synchronization
44: │   └── light_properties.py   # Scene-wide properties and custom data types
45: │
46: ├── operators/                # Logic and actions triggered by UI or viewport events
47: │   ├── assets.py             # Operations for importing library assets (Blockers, Bouncers)
48: │   ├── presets.py            # Rig generator operators (3-Point, Warm-Cool, Butterfly, etc.)
49: │   └── linking.py            # Collection and lighting relationship assignment handlers
50: │
51: ├── ui/                       # Visual layout and draw calls
52: │   ├── main_panel.py         # Main N-Panel sidebar containing light lists and linking panels
53: │   ├── properties_light.py   # Preview generation buttons and object lighting adjustments
54: │   └── menu_popup.py         # Floating quick-popup settings panel
55: │
56: └── utils/                    # Shared helper functions and rendering controllers
57:     ├── addon.py              # Preference retrieval helpers
58:     ├── icons.py              # Dynamic preview and icon cache management
59:     ├── detection.py          # Background handler for light-groups and mesh lights
60:     └── viewport_preview.py   # GPU rendering drawing handles and depsgraph updates</code></pre>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 2. Core Systems & Workflows ──</h2>
  
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8 text-xs">
    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-5 rounded-2xl">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-2 font-mono">1. Viewport Gizmo Interface</strong>
      Provides direct interactive controls drawn right next to selected lights. Instantly adjust light type, Area shapes (Square/Disk/Rectangle/Ellipse), Solo status, sizes, and beam spreads without having properties tabs open.
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-5 rounded-2xl">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-2 font-mono">2. GPU Linking Highlights System</strong>
      Utilizes Blender's GPU module shader pipelines (<code>GPUShader</code>) to render receiver/blocker outlines directly onto the viewport buffer during active Light/Shadow linking actions, avoiding undo stack bloat.
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-5 rounded-2xl">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-2 font-mono">3. Interactive Sky Rotation</strong>
      A modal viewport operator that rotates world environment mapping coordinates, Nishita Sun angles, or viewport HDRI values. Triggered via <code>Ctrl + Alt + RMB</code> and dragged horizontally.
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-5 rounded-2xl">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-2 font-mono">4. Geographic Sun & Sky</strong>
      Accepts decimal coordinates, Degree-Minute-Second DMS coordinates, or text-labeled maps to calibrate day/night cycles. Renders daily solar arc indicators and ground-horizon compass guides in the viewport.
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 3. Preview Rendering & Caching ──</h2>
  <p>
    To eliminate viewport stuttering and freezes when adjusting material properties, SLM implements three optimization structures:
  </p>

  <ul class="space-y-4 mb-8">
    <li class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Persistent Preview Scene Caching:</strong>
      A hidden scene (<code>.slm_preview_scene</code>) is kept alive containing camera, plane, and material blocks. Modifying shader nodes updates the material node tree but reuses the graphics pipeline, reducing render compiled times from <strong>~200ms to ~10ms</strong>.
    </li>
    <li class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Depsgraph Update Debouncing:</strong>
      Dragging exposure or color sliders registers timestamp offsets. The render routine waits for a <strong>0.4-second debounce window</strong> before triggering a redraw task, locking viewport navigation at a smooth 60 FPS.
    </li>
    <li class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Selection Isolation:</strong>
      Selecting an alternate light triggers instantly. The UI fetches existing thumbnails from cached storage immediately, delaying background renders until properties are actively tweaked.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 4. Viewport Shortcuts ──</h2>
  <p>
    Key interactions mapped inside the active viewport session:
  </p>
  
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Action</th>
        <th>Shortcut Command</th>
        <th>Context</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Quick Popup Menu</strong></td>
        <td><code>Y</code></td>
        <td>Viewport Selected Emitters</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Interactive HDRI Rotation</strong></td>
        <td><code>Ctrl + Alt + RMB</code> (Drag Mouse)</td>
        <td>Viewport Shaded Views</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Precision Adjustments</strong></td>
        <td>Hold <code>Shift</code> while dragging</td>
        <td>Active Modal Operators</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Stepped Snappings</strong></td>
        <td>Hold <code>Ctrl</code> while dragging</td>
        <td>Active Modal Operators</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Confirm modal coordinates</strong></td>
        <td><code>Left Click</code> or <code>Enter</code></td>
        <td>Active Modal Operators</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Cancel modal coordinates</strong></td>
        <td><code>Right Click</code> or <code>Escape</code></td>
        <td>Active Modal Operators</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 5. Developer API & RNA Custom Properties ──</h2>
  <p>
    For pipeline integration, script automations, or asset exporters, SLM registers custom RNA data blocks:
  </p>

  <h3>Custom Collection Attributes</h3>
  <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs font-mono mb-6">
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">coll.k_tools_rig_type</code> - Enum indicating spawned rig presets (3Point, Studio Duo, W-Cool, Rim, etc).</li>
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">coll.k_tools_lock_exposure</code> - Boolean toggle enabling exposure override.</li>
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">coll.k_tools_lock_exposure_val</code> - Float value (-10.0 to 10.0) driving exposure levels.</li>
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">coll.k_tools_lock_lg_val</code> - String setting target Light Group overrides.</li>
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">coll.k_tools_lock_ll_val</code> - Pointer property referencing Light Linking target collections.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Object State Caching Properties</h3>
  <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs font-mono mb-6">
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">obj["k_tools_original_exposure"]</code> - Float storing pre-override exposure value.</li>
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">obj["k_tools_original_lg"]</code> - String storing pre-override Light Group assignments.</li>
    <li><code class="text-amber-400">obj["k_tools_original_ll"]</code> - Pointer mapping pre-override Light Linking paths.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 6. Troubleshooting & FAQ ──</h2>

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      <strong>[WARNING] Viewport lag during slider manipulation:</strong>
      If adjusting exposure or colors causes micro-stuttering, ensure <strong>Cycles GPU</strong> is set as the active Preview Render Engine in Addon Preferences. Cycles performs asynchronous background renders, whereas EEVEE compiles shaders synchronously on Blender's main thread, causing frames to drop.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <ul class="space-y-6 mt-6 text-xs">
    <li>
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Q: Why is "No Shader Preview Rendered" showing?</strong>
      <p class="text-zinc-400">
        Shader previews require node-based materials. Ensure that the active emitter has "Use Nodes" enabled under Blender's shading editor. Previews are not compiled for standard inputs.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Q: A tagged Mesh Light is missing from the Outliner list?</strong>
      <p class="text-zinc-400">
        Ensure the mesh material has an active Emissive shader, and the mesh name or material name matches your preference keywords (e.g. <code>glow</code>, <code>emit</code>). You can also mark objects manually via the <strong>Mark as Mesh Light</strong> operator.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocLayout>
